  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 115 PM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nTuesday through Thursday will be dry. Max temps should be in the \nU60s/L70s plains with 50s in the valleys.\n\nBy Friday, temps will be similar to the days prior, but we will see \na chance of showers over the San Juans and possibly the far \nsoutheast plains.\n\nFor the weekend...Another trough is forecast to move across the \nWestern CONUS. Both the primary deterministic guidance products \n(EC/GFS) show this trough development, but vary in the intensity and \nlocation of the trough. GFS is more gung-ho with a stronger system \nwhile EC is farther north and quicker. As it stands now, it appears \nthe mountains along the divide should get precip with this system, \nand since these systems appear colder, we should see more snow than \nrain the the mtns. \\/Hodanish",
